ral homes are also being flooded in the South\nFork area.  The river gauge on the south fork of the Rio Grande\n(SRGC2) is rapidly rising, and forecast to crest at 9.2 feet by 1\nAM tonight, and slowly fall during the overnight hours.  The main\nstem of the Rio Grande will likely run high down toward Del\nNorte.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDel Norte, South Fork, Wagon Wheel Gap, Wolf Creek Pass and\nCreede.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-22T22:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO; Saguache, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3d025e343077c60bfd8f01d7a0415054feb8704b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3d025e343077c60bfd8f01d7a0415054feb8704b.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-22T23:54:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 222354 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 554 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flood Watch remains through the day Friday for the eastern San Juan mountains and the Upper Rio Grande Valley, with areal stream/river flooding and rock/mud slides possible. - Periods of moderate to heavy rain for the Continental Divide, tonight into early Friday,","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-22T06:48:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 220648 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1248 AM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-231300- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T01:56:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... A 